    {
      "title": "Judge clears way for Lindsay Clancy to be retried on murder charges",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/09/lindsay-clancy-judge-retrial",
      "description": "<p>Massachusetts judge rejects bid by Clancy’s attorneys to have the case against her dismissed</p><p>A Massachusetts judge cleared the way on Monday for Lindsay Clancy to be tried again on ⁠murder charges for killing her three young children at her home in 2023, saying a retrial would not unconstitutionally subject her to a ⁠double prosecution for the same ⁠crime.</p><p>Judge William ​Sullivan in Plymouth rejected a bid by Clancy’s attorneys to have the case against her dismissed. The judge on 4 September declared ⁠a mistrial after the jury reported that a holdout juror was preventing it from reaching a unanimous verdict.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/09/lindsay-clancy-judge-retrial\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-09T20:42:22"
    }
